    <h1>Choosing Chilli by Application: Hot Sauce, Chilli Oil &amp; Snack Seasoning</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The right chilli depends on what the finished product is scored on — heat, colour, aroma or all
      three. This guide maps the four common applications to the variety, SHU, form and mesh that suit
      each.
    </p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Hot sauce wants high heat (Sanying/Zidantou/Jixin, 20,000–50,000+
      SHU); chilli oil wants aroma (Erjingtiao) blended with heat; snack seasoning wants balanced heat
      and even dispersion (Seven-Star powder); seasoning blends want a controlled, consistent SHU window
      by variety.
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Hot sauce</h2>
    <p>
      Hot sauce is scored on heat and colour. Use high-heat varieties —
      <strong>Sanying, Zidantou or Jixin</strong> in the 20,000–50,000+ SHU band — usually as powder or
      flakes. Specify the variety and a precise SHU window; heat is non-linear, so "hot" is not a
      specification. See <a href="/guides/asta-colour-and-shu-heat-explained/">SHU explained</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Chilli oil and infused oil</h2>
    <p>
      Chilli oil is judged on fragrance as much as heat. The classic base is aromatic
      <strong>Erjingtiao</strong> (15,000–30,000 SHU), often blended with a heat variety such as
      Sanying or Jixin. Use <strong>flakes or segments</strong> for even infusion and to keep the
      aromatic surface intact — fine powder clouds the oil and fades faster.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Snack seasoning</h2>
    <p>
      Snack coating wants even, instant heat and colour dispersion across a large surface. Use
      <strong>Seven-Star</strong> (or a Sanying/Zidantou blend) at <strong>60–80 mesh powder</strong>,
      in a controlled SHU window. Powder disperses fastest, which is exactly what a dry snack seasoning
      needs.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Seasoning blends and spice mixes</h2>
    <p>
      Blends need a <strong>controlled, consistent SHU window by variety</strong>, plus a defined colour
      (ASTA) where colour matters. Specify the variety, the SHU window, the mesh and the ASTA — heat,
      colour and flavour are independent, and a blend drifts unless each is pinned. See
      <a href="/guides/paprika-chilli-buying-guide/">how to specify and source</a>.
    </p>

