    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">The Author's Take</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Position:</strong> In my view, application selection is really three questions — what is
      the product scored on, what SHU window delivers it, and which variety holds that window
      consistently — and the answer is a blend, not a single chilli.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reasoning:</strong> Heat, colour and aroma rarely all peak in one variety, so serious
      products blend. A hot sauce pairs a heat variety with a colour/aroma variety; a chilli oil pairs
      aromatic Erjingtiao with heat. The buyers who get consistent product are the ones who name the
      varieties and the window, not the ones who order "hot chilli".
    </p>
    <p>
